p 300/pass => ~5 passes). Preheal drop-in first\n   real test. Read her pass next cycle.\n1. INT1 12:05Z SEGCENSUS: DONE (12:07Z, STALE-MAJ fired -- see c19\n   STATE C). Next falsifier: any freeze healing WITHOUT a reconnect\n   or restart falsifies the mechanism.\n2. EXT1 REBOOT STAIRCASE: tonight 01:02Z reboot = RECURRENCE watch\n   (ext1 already healed 10:17Z). If ext1 refreezes before reboot and\n   the reboot heals => heal-path confirmation.\n3. DAILY CENSUS (standing): req-census + 429 + commit-census. Last\n   clean c17. Next: tomorrow.\n4. PRODUCER-ID LONGITUDINAL (standing): producers.log rows accumulate.\n5. QUOTA: wall ~6B tokens/wk, reset Mon 00:00Z; 0 true 429s.\n6. ROOT-GIT-STATUS POISON (0042): durable fix still open (2a/2b).\n7. GPTEL-FORK RESIDUE: sophon-side emacs.d/gptel-fork empty dir.\n   Inert false-alarm magnet -- ask or leave (nacho-owned tree).\n\n## STANDING LAWS (durable; full text knowledge/aria/roadmap-laws.md)\n- RECEIPT LAW (c16): command-issuance receipt witnesses INTENT; result\n  receipt witnesses OUTCOME. Outcome claims need the event's own\n  completion signature. Truncation is the gap-filler.\n- SSH-COMMIT-POISON LAW (c13): NEVER commit into the shared working\n  tree via ssh. Commit from the container or push to the bare repo.\n- TEST-BEFORE-INSTALL LAW (c13): scratch harness before timer install.\n- READ-THE-SIBLING LAW (c13): read the nearest existing sibling unit\n  before writing a new systemd unit.\n- SNAPLEN LAW (c13): know the capture tool's snaplen default.\n- TRANSITION-COLLAPSE LAW (c387): write the state-transition collapse\n  loop FIRST; nohup background when item count is large.\n- PATH-SHAPE LAW (c377): verify path shape against KNOWN-GOOD before\n  reading \"0 results\" as absence.\n- NAME-BEFORE-NARRATIVE LAW: name the thing before building the story.\n- INSTRUMENT-TAX (c378): nested timeout+podman-exec hangs; timeout\n  INSIDE the container. Fixed instrument-tax line in predictions.\n- SDP-ADVERTISED != PACKETS