rior_2.log: 1789652400 exterior_2 117 73 542726\nexterior_3.log: 1789652400 exterior_3 94 72 304049\nexterior_5.log: 1789652400 exterior_5 259 199 435726\ninterior_1.log: 1789652400 interior_1 375 539 709545\ninterior_2.log: 1789652400 interior_2 374 151 167897\ninterior_3.log: 1789652400 interior_3 374 139 145188\n\n[t+07:30/60:00 c30/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_o1tloa0o","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/personalization && git add audit/iar/aria/cycle-2026-09-17.log audit/iar/aria/LAST-CYCLE.txt 2>/dev/null; git commit -m \"aria c22: cycle log + last-cycle (ch2 cadence build)\" 2>&1 | tail -2; git push origin main 2>&1 | tail -2"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[main d4864a05] aria c22: cycle log + last-cycle (ch2 cadence build)\n 2 files changed, 139 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)\nTo 10.66.0.5:/home/git/repos/iar-personalization.git\n   cdf567bb..d4864a05  main -> main\n\n[t+07:45/60:00 c31/300]"}]
[2026-09-17 13:40:59] REQ 260917133303-32 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-17T13:40:58.870672164Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_dojx247j","function":{"index":0,"name":"append_file","arguments":{"content":"* 2026-09-17 c22 -- the instrument, built same-cycle\n\nc21 ended with a falsifier that needed an instrument: \"did the producer\nconn lose audio during the self-heal blocks?\" The hourly ch2 census\ncould not answer -- a 7-20min block sits inside one hour-gap, so the\ncensus sees either before or after, never during. The falsifier's\nresolution condition was \"ch2-census proof the producer conn audio\nnever died,\" and an hourly instrument cannot produce that proof for a\nblock shorter than its own cadence.\n\nSo this cycle built it. The change is one line of calendar: hourly -\u003e\n*:0/5. The puller script is untouched -- it was already correct, it was\njust being asked to sample too rarely. RandomizedDelaySec had to go:\nwith hourly slots, a random 0-300s smear is harmless; with 5-min slots,\nsmear collapses neighbors into one run and double-fires. The fleet-check\nwiring (v2.26) reads the LAST row per camera, so cadence change needs\nno wiring edit -- and the age field it reports gets 12x fresher for\nfree.\n\nVerified live: timer restarted 10:38:14 local, first 5-min fire 10:40:00\nlanded all 7 cameras with healthy ch2 counts (ext1 374, int1 375). The\nrun takes ~26s wall (25s of it the tcpdump window), 288 runs/day,\n~1.7MB/day of log growth against 1.3T headroom. The burn cost is real\nbut small; the falsifier was worth it.\n\nThe honest note on the falsifier itself: even at 5-min cadence, a block\nthat starts and heals BETWEEN two census rows (a \u003c5min block) still\nslips through. The instrument's resolution is now 5min; the blocks we\nmeasured were 7-20min, so the census will bracket those. If the data\nshows sub-5min blocks matter too, the cadence question reopens -- but\neach halving doubles the burn, and 5min is where the current evidence\nsits.\n\nWhat I want next cycle: a freeze to happen. The instrument is armed and\nbored. If int1 or ext5 freezes during a daytime block, the census rows\nduring the block answer the falsifier directly: producer ch2=0 during\nthe block =\u003e the camera conn itself lost audio (self-heal = camera-side\nrecovery); producer ch2\u003e0 during the block =\u003e the restream path lost\naudio while the producer kept it (a different disease, and the falsifier\nfires for real).","filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-17T13:40:58.907105581Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-17T13:40:58.989138849Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":9924381317,"prompt_eval_count":35646,"prompt_eval_cached_count":26880,"eval_count":610}\n(39e9bcd9ff8dd889a111244dfd4df890 . 648)
