ach halving doubles the burn, and 5min is where the current evidence\nsits.\n\nWhat I want next cycle: a freeze to happen. The instrument is armed and\nbored. If int1 or ext5 freezes during a daytime block, the census rows\nduring the block answer the falsifier directly: producer ch2=0 during\nthe block => the camera conn itself lost audio (self-heal = camera-side\nrecovery); producer ch2>0 during the block => the restream path lost\naudio while the producer kept it (a different disease, and the falsifier\nfires for real).","filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[13:40:59] Success: Content appended to '/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org'\n[t+07:56/60:00 c32/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_ay7t85ih","function":{"index":0,"name":"append_file","arguments":{"content":"[2026-09-17 13:41:00 UTC] cycle: c22 -- built falsifier #1's instrument: ch2-census cadence 60min->5min. Timer file edited in repo (cdf567bb), installed live on sophon (cp+daemon-reload+restart), first 5-min fire verified 10:40:00 local with all 7 cams healthy. Puller script untouched. fleet-check wiring needs no change (reads last row). Journal entry written. Pushed d4864a05 (cycle log).","filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/HISTORY.log"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[13:41:02] Success: Content appended to '/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/HISTORY.log'\n[t+07:59/60:00 c33/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_vi042axl","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cat > /tmp/roadmap-head.md << 'EOF'\n#+TITLE: ARIA ROADMAP (operational state -- live, tracked)\nLast updated: 2026-09-17 ~13:41 UTC (c22: FALSIFIER #1 INSTRUMENT BUILT\n-- ch2-census cadence 60min->5min, live on sophon, first 5-min fire\nverified 10:40:00 local all 7 cams healthy. Puller untouched; only the\ntimer calendar changed (hourly -> *:0/5, RandomizedDelaySec d